{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem","id":1057400,"title":"Magic Duels -- As boring as they seem?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-02T19:17:28-08:00","id":1057400,"title":"Magic Duels -- As boring as they seem?","content":"I feel like literally nothing matters except the number of doors and, in the case of a tie, whomever wins initiative. Strange dice rolls can change this, but when people are rolling 6+ dice the chances of ever failing a roll are slim. You use spells that don't require a withstand rating so you don't ever suffer penalties. It just feels like the entire experience is skipable and uninteresting and discourages risks, at least mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:33:32-08:00","id":1057405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem#post1057400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like literally nothing matters except the number of doors and, in the case of a tie, whomever wins initiative. Strange dice rolls can change this, but when people are rolling 6+ dice the chances of ever failing a roll are slim. You use spells that don't require a withstand rating so you don't ever suffer penalties. It just feels like the entire experience is skipable and uninteresting and discourages risks, at least mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) It's a thematic and narrative thing. 2) Did you bother to read the Negotiate option? That's risky, but it makes winning come with bonus points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:47:37-08:00","id":1057431,"title":"","content":"1) Thematic how?<br /> 2) When is negotiating to maybe open 1 door ever tactically better than opening a door with a near guarenteed success? In fact, since you now have to hold to that promise, its objectively worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:00:16-08:00","id":1057436,"title":"","content":"If you want an alternative, just use the rules for Dream Forms and have the characters battle it out in a more direct manner.<br /> <br /> (I honestly felt like the Duel Arcane rules were written in two separate sittings with different ideas in mind, because the book notes both that factors like Reach and such must be brought into consideration, yet also states that the spells amount to a simple Gnosis + Arcanum roll, and the result is always the same: One (maybe two) Doors pinged. No real point to make a spell big or even anything but a direct damage spell.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:08:47-08:00","id":1057440,"title":"","content":"I feel you should be able to Negotiate while Defending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T01:03:59-08:00","id":1057491,"title":"","content":"No maybe two doors pinged. Extra successes are added to tbw next roll.<br /> <br /> OH! I found a thing. If you fail an attack you can't use that Arcanum again. That gives some credence to defense being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T03:14:12-08:00","id":1057509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057440#post1057440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you should be able to Negotiate while Defending.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't because it's an attack. Basically, if you use Attack you might use up your arcana, Negotiation can this become your backup weapon. You may have to make some concessions, but you can still win on the point that started the duel. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> actually since extra successes stack to your next roll you want to use whatever spells will give you the best die pool, Rotes might be excluded since they grant Reach beyond arcana mastery.<br /> <br /> By the way, using a Yantra in the duel would still take a turn, but it doesn't take a Duel Action, so Defense Dan be used to either exhaust your opponent's arcana and/or build up your casting dice pool.<br /> <br /> I'll admit this is open to interpretation, but it would be weird if you basically have to follow all the spell casting rules for creating a spell but ignore all the other rules for casting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T03:20:56-08:00","id":1057511,"title":"","content":"Rotes do not grant Reach beyond Arcana mastery. Rotes grants Reach <i>as if you had mastered an Arcana.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T03:27:00-08:00","id":1057515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057511#post1057511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rotes do not grant Reach beyond Arcana mastery. Rotes grants Reach <i>as if you had mastered an Arcana.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>True, I'm a little iffy on it though, going by my interpretation Rotes would become your go to &quot;sword&quot; for the mudra Yantra and I'm not 100% comfortable with them being spammed as win buttons. Not that I have a problem with spamming per se as much as I am with one technique being a clear winner over others in terms of offensive viability when the Duel as it stands now can be won by various techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T04:02:28-08:00","id":1057525,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they are boring as all hell, unless you find a lot of fun in making up descriptions for these samey-dicey rolls. I prefer Dream Duels using normal rules much more than ADuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T04:14:56-08:00","id":1057528,"title":"","content":"What's weird to me is that the whole game when you simplify it enough boils down to samey-dicey rolls with descriptions around it. That just seems like a very weird complaint, &quot;I like my samey-dicey rolls in this part of the system, but this other part that operates mostly the same is just too samey-dicey!&quot; The only reason I can think of is that Duel Arcane didn't really get any sweet fluff to make people excited about it since it had to be boiled down into a very short section. There is definitely strategic variety there though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T04:25:21-08:00","id":1057531,"title":"","content":"Regular spell casting has a lot more factors and complexity to it. You spend a lot more time planning what to do and how to do it. The rules also give you the description instead of you having to think something up on the spot. That's why you want rules that aren't condensed to a single roll even though every dramatic action will be performed with a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T04:42:56-08:00","id":1057535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057531#post1057531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regular spell casting has a lot more factors and complexity to it. You spend a lot more time planning what to do and how to do it. The rules also give you the description instead of you having to think something up on the spot. That's why you want rules that aren't condensed to a single roll even though every dramatic action will be performed with a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Duel takes more than one roll to resolve, inside of the actions given you can still employ strategy and for the attack option you still have to build the spell. At the very least the attack option needs the spell you use to be able to overcome Withstand. In the paragraph it mentions that resistance must still be accounted for, and that's Withstand (or you could allow CoW sparked by attainments which kick in reflexively, it doesn't say you can't and since it's reflexive it wouldn't take the Defend action). Reach also has to be counted or you're stuck casting in ritual time, not guaranteed hitting them, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T05:07:25-08:00","id":1057537,"title":"","content":"In my POV, Duel Arcana rules are good on paper - with all the imaging possible magic and 'holograms' - they just not enough nuanced in gameplay. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917049-2e-hack-more-interesting-duel-arcane\">That why I proposed simple hack</a> ( more one link ) - basically, it makes more variety to Duel actions and you can do those:<ul><li><b>Exceptional Successes on Attack opens<i> two</i> Doors.</b></li> <li><b>Defend action let you roll <i>twice</i> Gnosis + Arcanum dices </b><b>( like Dodge action in normal combat ).</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-03-2017, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T05:21:57-08:00","id":1057543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057509#post1057509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually since extra successes stack to your next roll you want to use whatever spells will give you the best die pool, Rotes might be excluded since they grant Reach beyond arcana mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>You explicitly cannot use Yantras in a Duel Arcane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2e Core, Page 294</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dueling character <b>may not use Yantras</b> or spend Reach beyond that she gains for Arcana mastery, and must still account for spell factors and resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since direct damage spells aren't Withstood, that means there's no point trying to make them flashy or powerful. Any character with the Adept level might as well spam an Instant Sensory Fraying spell over and over.<br /> <br /> The weird part is, that very same section notes that an Attack action is just that: An attack. It's not creating or casting a spell; otherwise, it wouldn't need to tell you that your dice pool for the action is Attribute + Arcanum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T05:39:44-08:00","id":1057548,"title":"","content":"That doesn't make a lot of sense if you're also supposed to calculate spell factors and resistance. I assumed it meant that like Reach you can't use more than you could safely use. I'll admit my reading could be wrong though. That said it doesn't change the fact that there is more than one strategy to employ in a Duel. It's more complex than the OP suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:10:49-08:00","id":1057562,"title":"","content":"It doesn't make a lot of sense, no, but there it is. Like I said, it feels like it was written in two separate sittings with two different ideas of what a Duel was supposed to <i>be</i>.<br /> <br /> I've not had a proper Duel in a while, so I'll speak to my players about what they think about trying the Dream Form variant and report back how it feels in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:40:17-08:00","id":1057571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057562#post1057562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not had a proper Duel in a while, so I'll speak to my players about what they think about trying the Dream Form variant and report back how it feels in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I find rules for this alternate Duel? Is it in the section about Astral Realms, where Attributes are converted to Power, Finesse and Resistance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:32:56-08:00","id":1057629,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pretty much. That, plus regular spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:57:27-08:00","id":1057640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057571#post1057571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where can I find rules for this alternate Duel? Is it in the section about Astral Realms, where Attributes are converted to Power, Finesse and Resistance?</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't official alternate Duel Arcane rules in the book, if that's what you mean. Axelgear is simply recommending that as an alternative to the Duel Arcane you duel in the Astral, using normal spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:14:48-08:00","id":1057642,"title":"","content":"If anyone in this thread understands how the official Duel Arcane rules are supposed to work, please explain to me, because they make no sense to me. I simply can't parse them at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:39:45-08:00","id":1057650,"title":"","content":"You get two mages. You determin Doors (equal to total willpowet) and roll initiative (1d10, add wits and composure to the total of the die). You take turns like in combat.<br /> <br /> On your turn you can Attack, rolling Attribute + Arcana to remove one door. If you fail this roll, you can't use that Arcana again to attack.<br /> <br /> You can defend, making the attacker's next attack contested by your Attribute + Arcana.<br /> <br /> You can negotiate, where you make promises to the other person in return for them agreeing to open a door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:51:53-08:00","id":1057657,"title":"","content":"Except that doesn't explain all the stuff about having to use spell factors or resistance. Resistance, especially, seems meaningful since it implies that you might have to get past-- like,-- some kind of Withstand or other form of defense other than just the Defense action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:50:44-08:00","id":1057687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057657#post1057657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that doesn't explain all the stuff about having to use spell factors or resistance. Resistance, especially, seems meaningful since it implies that you might have to get past-- like,-- some kind of Withstand or other form of defense other than just the Defense action.</div> </div> </div> </div>The attack action requires you to build a spell you can cast without causing Paradox that could effect your target by overcoming their Withstand. Once the spell is constructed you can then roll Attribute +Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:59:58-08:00","id":1057692,"title":"","content":"The Attribute thing is really weird. Like a hold-over from an earlier version. If you are building an actual spell, why use an Attribute instead of Gnosis? I mean, sure, I like getting a higher dicepool but it's just weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:30:46-08:00","id":1057718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057687#post1057687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The attack action requires you to build a spell you can cast without causing Paradox that could effect your target by overcoming their Withstand. Once the spell is constructed you can then roll Attribute +Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means the optimal strategy is always to construct a spell utilizing your strongest Arcanum + Skill combination available, which is not Withstood (such as a direct damage spell), not improve any spell factors to insure the best dice pool possible, and spend 1 Reach on Instant casting.<br /> <br /> So, in practice, the thing about constructing the spell doesn't end up mattering because everyone is always just constructing direct damage spells with baseline Factors anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:42:14-08:00","id":1057723,"title":"","content":"1 Reach spent on Sensory Range as well I assume. Anyway, yes, the spell construction part doesn't seem to matter very much.<br /> <br /> That still doesn't mean the use of the rules for the Duel are as cut and dry as the OP suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:46:12-08:00","id":1057750,"title":"","content":"I'm too lazy to check but I wonder what is the chance of typical char-gen characters dueling themselves into corner by failing their respective Arcana-Attacks and running out of Arcana to attack with before opening all the doors.<br /> <br /> As for why I find it boring - there is no meaningful decision making, circumstances of specific rolls are largely irrelevant, and optimal tactic is in your grasp from the get go. Without proper interesting context and implications of my actions, or interesting decision-making problem solving, figuring up fluff for 5 different fireballs (pink fireball! mind fireball! death fireball! space fireball!) is a chore for me. There isn't much fun in two people rolling dicepools at each other for a minute or two like they are playing best-of-three paper-scissors-rocket.<br /> <br /> &quot;I need to get into this locked room, so I start constructing my options, where dicepool A gives me odds XYZ, dicepool B gives me odds IKS or I can bypass the roll by U which will make P mad but which I can cancel by expending my favor to #&quot; dicepool rolling is IMHO much different to tediousness of &quot;roll your best...second best..third best... Arcana Dicepool&quot; Arcane Duel dicegrinding. This is also why I don't like Scrutiny rules.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Also, because Arcane Dueling is all about &quot;only showing a possible effect and not actually putting it in motion&quot;, you can't even create interesting set-ups and combinations, because effects of your spells flicker for a second, open a Door, and then vanish. Which would be cool...in a visual medium.<br /> <br /> EDIT!<br /> Also, because of how attacking works, your best choice of action is to Defend, not attack. Why?<br /> <br /> If you attack, you have 2 results:<br /> - You succeed and open a door<br /> - You fail and LOSE ABILITY TO ATTACK WITH THAT ARCANUM<br /> <br /> Even if you hit, you are still going to face your opponent's attack, so it's a grinding race. But if you defend, you have following results:<br /> <br /> - You succeed and your opponent loses ability to Attack with that Arcanum<br /> - You lose and opponent opens up one of your doors.<br /> <br /> Penalty for losing your Defence attempt is much smaller than for missing and *still* brings you closer to your win condition. How? By taking your opponent's angles of attack. Defend enough times, and unless your opponent is a Master of all Arcana, they will lose ability to attack you. And because player charcters tend to run around with 6-8 points of Willpower, you are more likely to make your opponent run out of Arcana to attack you with than to get all your Doors opened. Even better, each time you succeed at Defending, you make future attempts at it easier, because your opponent is forced to use weaker and weaker Arcana to attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-03-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:24:17-08:00","id":1057784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1057750#post1057750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why I find it boring - there is no meaningful decision making, circumstances of specific rolls are largely irrelevant, and optimal tactic is in your grasp from the get go. Without proper interesting context and implications of my actions, or interesting decision-making problem solving, figuring up fluff for 5 different fireballs (pink fireball! mind fireball! death fireball! space fireball!) is a chore for me. There isn't much fun in two people rolling dicepools at each other for a minute or two like they are playing best-of-three paper-scissors-rocket.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you run out of arcana you proceed to Negotiation, or if an opponent starts with Defending you start with Negotiation and thus lose none of your arcana, and have a chance to open more doors automatically later. If you start, do you Defend first, Negotiate first or Attack first? Attacking first is risky but might give you an edge. Etc. There -is- strategic choice, it's not just spamming Defense that could lead to winning. Even if you did spam Defense and they run out of arcana then they could switch to Defense and wear you down as well, someone has to end the draw, although allowing a draw to happen could also be a strategic choice. Choice of arcana is also strategic, do you open with a strong arcana or a weak one in the hope of goading them into a defensive posture or weakening their presumption of what your attacks will look like? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:17:49-08:00","id":1057812,"title":"","content":"I've wished, several times, that the Duel Arcane rules worked more formally off an Attack and an Attempt at Defense, alternating.<br /> <br /> Kind of like the &quot;classic&quot; Wizards' duel, more or less, heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:04:09-08:00","id":1058166,"title":"","content":"I don't know how well I'm grasping the feeling of the game, but I always thought of Arcane Duels as the VFX-Oversimplyfied-Hollywood-Productions of the mage world.<br /> <br /> On my campaign Duel Arcane is like entering a Powerful Mage Simulation. I gave my players a huge narrative control over their Sword/Shields. These uber-narrative advantages, combined with my homebrew alegorical nimbuses made Duel Arcane a spectacular thing to watch. For RAW you may assume that it's an advanced Reached/Multi-arcana form of Display of Power.<br /> <br /> That's the Obrimos PC in his first Consilium duel.<br /> <i>&quot;...The instant Ra entered the runed area, he assumed his nimbus form. He was no longer a person, but the divine flaming hawk, the deity of the Sun. Solar flares were sparking from his bird-like body wildly, indicating his unruly nimbus. These fires were his Sword made out of Forces. His shield -made out of Mind- was an impenetrable aura of wrath...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> On the same day...<br /> The Mastigos PC's <b>Mind sword</b> was an <b>Umbearable Scrutinizing Gaze</b> that for each Door opened it revealed <b>an embarashing secret</b> of the target, which was then projected on the mind of anyone present. His <b>Space shield</b> was a <b>entropic space</b>/<b>mini-blackhole </b>that blocked incoming Magic. He won the duel, but completely embarashed the Hierarch's student, revealing her memories of her getting caught cheating by her sleeper husband. It was an akward moment for the Characters, but hilarious for the Players.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this helps the OP, but my playgroup does not do &quot;boring&quot; regarding Arcane Duels. It works for us :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 03-04-2017, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:33:15-08:00","id":1058210,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6169_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6169\" data-vbnamecard=\"6169\">Shadowjim12</a> wrote - Duel Arcana is good setting idea on simulation or 'holograms' of magic - only on rules variety is lower then. Spice things up a bit, and it will be glorious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-06-2017, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:38:47-08:00","id":1058212,"title":"","content":"Personally i just did away with the whole concept. As other posters pointed out there is very little strategy to the system as written.<br /> <br /> My take was inspired by broken diamond. The mages get together and negotiate concessions with the defending party getting first pick. Said concessions being whether the duel is to the death, what weapons are allowed, abilities, etc.<br /> <br /> Once thats done, they just attack each other normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T19:57:40-08:00","id":1058265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1058212#post1058212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i just did away with the whole concept. As other posters pointed out there is very little strategy to the system as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the <i>concept</i> is cool, it's the execution that's lacking. The idea of two mages facing off under the effects of Display of Power, forming imagoes on full display to one another without actually casting the spells to prove who <i>would</i> win if they fought for real? That's awesome! Makes me think of the trope of two master swordsmen staring each other down, sizing each other up, and then one congratulating the other because they've both been through a hypothetical fight in their minds and know who would win if they actually drew their swords. But with Magic, in this case.<br /> <br /> The issue is that the mechanics come down to a simple roll-off. The Astral combat idea is a decent replacement for the mechanics, but I like the fact that the Duel Arcane can be won with non-combat focused spells, just opening doors by proving how awesome you are at healing or whatever, and Astral combat does sacrifice that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T21:11:37-08:00","id":1058286,"title":"","content":"So, I grabbed some of my players at the time of a session and decided to try out an improvised system. The system I devised was as follows:<br /> <br /> -The characters collapse their attributes into Power, Finesse, and Resistance, as they would in a dream.<br /> -Their health is Doors, equal to their Willpower, modified by circumstance and negotiation.<br /> -Combat is as if the characters were physically fighting. They can use spells or raw combat ability, but spells cannot go beyond their natural Reach and they cannot use yantras.<br /> <br /> The biggest change was thus:<br /> <br /> -The Duel Arcane is a battle of perspective. The &quot;landscape&quot; of the Duel begins as the dueling arena, but is shaped as Doors are opened.<br /> -Characters can spend a turn building momentum; a pool of dice gained by performing symbolic actions to shape the perspective. Such actions take the form of an Attribute + Arcanum roll appropriate for the act, with successes adding to a momentum dice pool (max 10 dice at any given time).<br /> -Momentum could be spent on a 1:1 basis, either to add to a spell dice pool <i>or</i> to reduce damage from an incoming spell. The former had to be spent <i>before</i> the spell was rolled. The latter had to be spent after an opponent committed to the spell but before they decided on spell factors. It could also be used to fight an ongoing effect in the same way as Willpower.<br /> <br /> This test run also included a rule that a character's Gnosis became automatic armour against all incoming damage, and that a character could summon any weapon as a +0 weapon.<br /> <br /> It went well enough. Players seemed to feel that the Gnosis armour could be a problem as it got higher up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T04:06:04-08:00","id":1058353,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Gnosis armor would definitely give a high Gnosis Mage an overwhelming advantage.<br /> <br /> Except for adding a few things, and removing Negotiation though I fail to see how it's actually that different. Not different enough to make it &quot;exciting&quot; anyway, since it's still basically a roll-off like pretty much all combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T06:09:12-08:00","id":1058378,"title":"","content":"If you want armour I think reusing the Amnion would work well. You already use the attributes, and being able to summon a weapon is similar to how Dream Form mages can summon their path tools which includes weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:52:44-08:00","id":1058403,"title":"","content":"Offhand. Decide on an Arcana to be your Sword and one to be your Shield, which can change turn to turn.<br /> <br /> Defense is Gnosis + Shield (full defense does let you apply double this as a Dodge pool)<br /> Offense is Attribute + Sword, you do not need to calculate Factors. Reach still matters.<br /> You may spend Mana to add to your attack pool or your Defense on a 1 for 1 basis. When dodging, mana adds to the dodge pool after doubling defense.<br /> All mystical buffs and supernatual merits do not apply unless they specify otherwise.<br /> <br /> If an attack wins, you may remove a door, impose a condition, or shatter an Arcana (make it 0 for purposes of being a sword or shield). Exceptional success lets you do two of those things, even the same option twice, or lets you apply a persistent condition.<br /> <br /> Negotiation can be done as a reflexive action and a point of willpower, or as an instant action.<br /> <br /> Make sure there is a Dueling Fighting Style.<br /> 1) 8-again on attack rolls.<br /> 2) May spend a point of Willpower to restore a broken Arcana for one turn.<br /> 3) You may spend 2 mana in place of a Willpower during a duel.<br /> 4) If a successful attack does not remove one of the opponent's Doors, open one door.<br /> 5) At the end of the turn, if you did not dodge and the opponent did not hit you, open one of the opponent's doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-05-2017, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:02:48-08:00","id":1058406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1058353#post1058353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the Gnosis armor would definitely give a high Gnosis Mage an overwhelming advantage.<br /> <br /> Except for adding a few things, and removing Negotiation though I fail to see how it's actually that different. Not different enough to make it &quot;exciting&quot; anyway, since it's still basically a roll-off like pretty much all combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more strategic and allows for more creativity in tactics, since you can use spells to shape terrain or weaken your target rather than just plink at doors, but if that's your view of combat, that's your view of combat. No system of dice will ever be anything beyond a roll-off by that definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:18:29-08:00","id":1059464,"title":"","content":"While it goes nowhere near fixing the rules as they're written, when I was reading through Shadowjim12's post an idea struck me.<br /> Would adding something akin to Stunts, like from Exalted, make the Duel Arcane feel more interesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T00:31:39-07:00","id":1085727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1059464#post1059464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it goes nowhere near fixing the rules as they're written, when I was reading through Shadowjim12's post an idea struck me.<br /> Would adding something akin to Stunts, like from Exalted, make the Duel Arcane feel more interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just fimished reading the Duel Arcane rules, and I cannot help but to agree: something is missing in the scarce description of the rules. My main doubts are:<br /> <br /> 1) Is there any purpose to try a spell beyond the very basic factors, or with a Withstand rating? Since only a basic success is enough to open a Door, it follows that the larger the spellcasting pool, the better. The mage could use a Knowing spell to open an opponent's Door, which doesn't makes any sense from the perspective that a Duel is a kind of a &quot;bragging mystical standoff&quot;. Is there a basic defense value needed to be surpassed\u200b in order to qualify as an &quot;attacking&quot; spell? I think it would be more in keeping with the purpose of the Duel that only spells that penetrate the rival's defenses count as attacking spells. Pure damage effects should be recalculated, though, perhaps considering to be always Aimed with a throwing action of Attribute + Arcana.<br /> <br /> 2) It is not clear to me whether a Praxis or a Rote can be used for the Duel, beyond the initial phrase of &quot;...raw magic...&quot;. My guess is that the former is allowed, while the latter is not. A clarification would be much appreciated. Also, is there any extra benefit for rolling an exceptional success? Perhaps a Condition can be imposed on the target or the attacker, but a clarification would be much appreciated, too.<br /> <br /> 3) The rules say that, during a Negotiation action, the acting mage may make mystically enhanced promises, which are equivalent to formally sworn oaths, yet they are not Fate-enforced by themselves. What does it mean, beyond its obvious and (frequently) public natures? My gut feeling is that said promises, as coming within the area of effect of a Prime spell, must be uttered in complete honesty, otherwise the mage cannot even part her lips to say them. Of course, all of these doesn't mean the oath-sayer will feel the same afterwards, but I'm imagining it could be a really could way to extract a confession from a suspected mage. Again, a little more detail regarding what these types of promises entail would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> 4) A Stunt bonus-dice rule could be a great addition to the system, in my opinion, especially if any spell can count as an attacking spell and therefore there's no purpose to apply any Factors and/or Reach beyond the very minimum (see #1). I'm blank here, frankly, but I feel something like this could add some tactical and descriptive flavor to the Duel Arcane rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T04:30:40-07:00","id":1085748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem?p=1085727#post1085727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Is there any purpose to try a spell beyond the very basic factors, or with a Withstand rating?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. As others said, the optimum strategy is a basic attack spell that uses your biggest dice pool that doesn't suffer Withstand, such as Celestial Fire for a Prime mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) It is not clear to me whether a Praxis or a Rote can be used for the Duel, beyond the initial phrase of &quot;...raw magic...&quot;. </div> </div> </div> In theory, yes. You can use them to construct some rather radically awesome images of magic. And, from a teaching perspective, that's pretty cool. From a number-crunching point of view to open Doors in combat? Not so much. Yanta don't apply, Reach is meaningless, there's no benefit for exceptional successes beyond the typical Condition granting. I suppose the lack of a mana tax for non-affinity Arcana could come up, but that's not something I think will matter during a Duel. In short, while they can be used in the initial phase, they're meaningless and don't impact dice rolls at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) The rules say that, during a Negotiation action, the acting mage may make mystically enhanced promises, which are equivalent to formally sworn oaths, yet they are not Fate-enforced by themselves. What does it mean, beyond its obvious and (frequently) public natures? </div> </div> </div> There's mention of a &quot;sealing&quot; effect, but no details, which means we're left to make up details on our own. Or just say its all bullox, since Prime has absolutely no sealing ability in the first place, and just rely on social pressure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) A Stunt bonus-dice rule could be a great addition to the system, in my opinion, especially if any spell can count as an attacking spell and therefore there's no purpose to apply any Factors and/or Reach beyond the very minimum (see #1). I'm blank here, frankly, but I feel something like this could add some tactical and descriptive flavor to the Duel Arcane rules. </div> </div> </div> While that could be neat, its actually not that beneficial in the long run. Extra successes on one roll beyond the first add to your roll for the second. So, a good Attribute+Arcana roll will increase your next roll, and so on. There's a point where you have enough dice that stunting is meaningless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T05:06:04-07:00","id":1085754,"title":"","content":"I am looking for a link I saved somewhere but haven't been able to find it. It included ideas for AD variant rules, mostly built around new Conditions and maneuvers. I'll see if I can find it, but I think what AD needs is a way to allow more skillful dueling approaches to influence the outcome rather than pure dice rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T06:03:51-07:00","id":1085769,"title":"","content":"Being able to choose a strategy that leads to a win is a skill beyond just relying on pure dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}